+    target = " ".join(map(str, inst["target_logs"]))
+    statement = f"""t-MULTIPLE DISCRETE LOGARITHM IN EXACT CRT COORDINATES
+
+All indices are 0-based. Let q={q}, a prime, and let
+N={inst['modulus_N']} be the product of the n={n} distinct primes printed
+below. For coordinate j, h_j is a unit of exact order q modulo p_j.
+
+An exponent-coordinate vector e=(e_0,...,e_{{n-1}}) over F_q represents the
+unique unit x modulo N satisfying x = h_j^e_j (mod p_j) for every j. Thus
+multiplication of represented group elements adds their coordinate vectors
+modulo q. This is an exact CRT representation, not floating-point data.
+
+The n modular bases g_0,...,g_{{n-1}} are given by the COLUMNS of the matrix A
+below: A[j][i] is the exponent of h_j in the jth CRT residue of g_i. The
+target beta has the displayed log-coordinate vector y and the independently
+displayed residues. The bases are promised to be independent elements of
+order q, so exactly one bounded exponent tuple exists.
+
+CRT components:
+{factor_rows}
+
+Base-log matrix A over F_q (n rows, n entries per row):
+{matrix_rows}
+
+Target log-coordinate vector y:
