-The native problem is Definition 2 of Fu, Bao, Shi and Wang,
-"t-multiple discrete logarithm problem and solving difficulty"
-(arXiv:1605.04870).  The generator constructs a direct product C_q^t inside
-the units modulo a composite N, samples its coordinate vector first, and then
-computes the target.  Primality and direct-product independence are established
-during construction; the checker itself only needs exact modular arithmetic.
+The group is a CRT product of prime-field subgroups of common prime order q.
+An instance is emitted in the exact logarithmic coordinate system used in
+Section 4, equations (3)--(4), of arXiv:1605.04870. Generation samples the
+exponent witness first and applies an invertible rank-one perturbation; it
+never solves the emitted instance.
