+
+NOTES = r"""
+Definition and easy cases. Section 3, Definition 2 fixes t-MDLP as finding the
+bounded exponent tuple (k_1,...,k_t) in a product of modular bases. Its
+non-degeneracy condition requires no nontrivial power of one base to lie in the
+subgroup generated by the others. Section 4, Theorem 1 identifies the common-
+exponent CRT collapse, Theorem 2 identifies projection to smaller MDLPs, and
+equations (3)-(4) explicitly linearize the multiplicative equation with
+discrete logarithms. The paper's stated exhaustive cost and claim that index
+calculus is unsuitable are not a distributional hardness theorem. An inverse
+generator therefore cannot honestly claim Track A merely from those passages.
+
+Construction. The modulus is represented by its exact CRT factors p_j. Each
+p_j has a displayed element h_j of prime order q. A vector e in F_q^n denotes
+the unique modular unit whose jth CRT residue is h_j**e_j. Choose a row vector
+v and set A=I+1*v^T with 1+sum(v_i) nonzero. The matrix determinant lemma makes
+A invertible. Sample distinct exponents k first and emit y=A*k. The columns of
+A are therefore independent order-q bases, so Definition 2 has one and only
+one bounded answer. The certificate is known by inverse generation.
+
+Track B. Equations (3)-(4) make generic exact Gaussian elimination available
+in O(n^3) field operations; the module runs and reports it as the reference
+algorithm. A second mechanical method tries every scalar shift in O(qn).
+Recognizing A-I as rank one instead gives y=k+s*1 and recovers s from two dot
+products, in at most 4n field operations. The shipping preset keeps this at
+the 300-operation cap while making elimination and scalar enumeration far too
+large to execute without tools.
+
+Attack handling. The sampled witness is conditioned only against a negligible
+set of conspicuous scalar shifts. Target-as-answer, diagonal-only, greedy
+forward substitution, 64 deterministic scalar restarts, and an average-shift
+ansatz are tested on eight seeds. Bases are not divided into planted and decoy
+populations: every entry comes from the same rank-one identity. Coordinate and
+generator relabellings are canonicalized by the unique exceptional entry in
+each row and column.
+""".strip()
