codex
Built and locally verified the Track B generator, but it is not yet shippable because the required OpenRouter oracle pool is unavailable.

Key results:

- Full paper reviewed; Definition 2, Theorems 1–2, and equations (3)–(4) determine the construction. The paper does not justify Track A distributional hardness. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.04870)
- Inverse CRT construction guarantees a unique witness.
- Theorem 1 common-exponent collapses and Theorem 2 single-coordinate projections are explicitly excluded.
- G1–G8 pass.
- G9 size limits pass: 444 characters, 74 elements, 296 operations.
- Reference Gaussian elimination: 418,877 field operations.
- Every oracle request returned HTTP 403: “Key limit exceeded”; therefore G9 and the hardening verdict remain pending.

